<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Event Hub — Gather, Learn, Repeat</title>
</head>
<body>

  <header>
    <h1>Event Hub</h1>
    <nav>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#upcoming-events">Upcoming Events</a></li>
        <li><a href="#past-events">Past Events</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>

    <section id="upcoming-events">
      <h2>Upcoming Events</h2>

      <article>
        <h3>Midnight Pancake Debugging</h3>
        <p>
          Bring a laptop and an appetite. We pair up on stubborn bugs until
          they crack, then reward ourselves with an unreasonable amount of
          pancakes. Beginners are genuinely welcome — no question is too small.
        </p>
        <p>Date: Friday, 13 March · 9:00 PM · The Waffle Annex</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Analog Photography Walk</h3>
        <p>
          A slow morning wandering the old warehouse district with film
          cameras and zero rush. We'll talk light meters, happy accidents,
          and why grain is having a moment again. Loaner cameras available.
        </p>
        <p>Date: Saturday, 4 April · 8:30 AM · Riverside Gate</p>
      </article>

    </section>

    <section id="past-events">
      <h2>Past Events</h2>

      <article>
        <h3>Retro Arcade Tournament</h3>
        <p>
          Sixty-four players, one creaky cabinet, and a final match that
          lasted longer than the pizza queue. We raised enough for two new
          community laptops and crowned a champion who had never played before.
        </p>
        <p>Date: 18 October · The Basement Arcade</p>
        <img
          src="https://cdn.freecodecamp.org/curriculum/labs/past-event1.jpg"
          alt="Players gathered around laptops and screens during a community coding session"
        >
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Storytelling Under the Stars</h3>
        <p>
          Five speakers, one open field, and a projector powered by a very
          brave extension cord. Topics ranged from migrating birds to
          migrating databases. Blankets were essential.
        </p>
        <p>Date: 2 August · Hilltop Meadow</p>
        <img
          src="https://cdn.freecodecamp.org/curriculum/labs/past-event2.jpg"
          alt="A speaker on stage addressing a seated audience at an evening event"
        >
      </article>

    </section>

  </main>

</body>
</html>
